  organName: Stomach & Intestines
  bodySystem: Digestive
  normalWeight: 1200
  description: J-shaped muscular organ and enteric tract responsible for chemical
    digestion and nutrient absorption.
  arterialSupply: Celiac trunk (left gastric, splenic, common hepatic branches) and
    Mesenteric arteries.
  innervation: Enteric nervous system with Vagus nerve parasympathetic input.
  clinicalFunction: Secretes gastric acid (HCl) and pepsin; peristaltic churning
    into chyme.
  commonPathology: Peptic ulcer disease, GERD, gastritis, Crohn's disease, colorectal
    cancer.
